Source: fido-daemon
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Fido Daemon Team <noreply@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/gatebridgeapp/fido2-android-bridge
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/gatebridgeapp/fido2-android-bridge.git

Package: fido-daemon
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, python3 (>= @PYMIN@) | python3.11, python3-cffi, systemd, udev, passwd, adduser
Description: Remote WebAuthn Android bridge daemon
 Linux daemon that bridges local WebAuthn login requests to a remote Android
 phone over an end-to-end encrypted (Noise) WebSocket relay, presenting a
 virtual FIDO2 security key. Private keys stay inside the phone's hardware
 enclave; neither the daemon nor the relay ever sees plain text.